Third-party components
----------------------

E-Signer uses the following components. Each remains under its own license; the AGPL-3.0 does not
change their terms.

- EU Digital Signature Service (DSS) 6.1, European Commission - GNU LGPL 2.1
  https://github.com/esig/dss
  Used unmodified as separate libraries.
- Inter font 4.1, The Inter Project Authors - SIL Open Font License 1.1
  https://github.com/rsms/inter
  core/src/main/resources/fonts/Inter-Regular.ttf, unmodified, draws the text of visible signatures and
  is embedded in signed PDFs. The license is next to it in Inter-LICENSE.txt.
- Apache PDFBox 2.0 - Apache License 2.0
- Bouncy Castle (bcprov, bcpkix) - MIT-style Bouncy Castle License
- Kotlin standard library and kotlinx.coroutines, JetBrains - Apache License 2.0
- Compose Multiplatform and Skiko, JetBrains and Google - Apache License 2.0
- Material Design icons, Google - Apache License 2.0
  A few icons are copied as path data in app/src/main/kotlin/sh/yetkin/esigner/app/ui/AppIcons.kt.
- SLF4J - MIT License
- Further transitive dependencies of DSS (Apache Commons, Jakarta XML Binding and others) under
  their own open source licenses; `./gradlew :app:dependencies` lists them.

Packaged builds include a Java runtime from Eclipse Temurin (OpenJDK 21), licensed under the
GNU GPL v2 with the Classpath Exception.

Bundled certificates
--------------------

core/src/main/resources/trust/ contains the public root certificates of Turkish qualified trust
service providers. They are public data published by their issuers; anchors.properties records the
source and SHA-256 digest of each.

Protocol references
-------------------

The Kamu SM time-stamp "identity" header (core/.../Timestamping.kt) is an independent
implementation of the request format, written with the open source project
KilimcininKorOglu/kamusm-go as a protocol reference. No code was copied from it.
